1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
That squeal only when you're
backing out isn't your imagination.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:09,000
One side, one direction — quiet
the rest of the day, loud in reverse.

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:15,000
One clue: a small wear-indicator tab
that only touches the rotor one way.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:21,000
Ignore it long enough and that tab
wears through — squeal can turn to grind.

5
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:26,000
Don't guess which side, or how
much pad you've got left.

6
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Worth checking before it gets bigger.
Stop by — Nick's Tire & Auto.
